### Strategic Reserve — the journal entry's panel.
###
### je_strategic_reserve.txt attaches the three named roots at the foot of
### this file:
###   widget_je_strategic_reserve_overview   container 1   te_st_res_overview_panel
###   widget_je_strategic_reserve_inventory  container 2   te_st_res_status_sections
###   widget_je_strategic_reserve_reference  container 3   te_st_res_reference_sections
### The entry's status text sits between the overview and the inventory, and
### its two shared buttons (Cycle Step Size, Reset Reserve Rates) between the
### inventory and How the Strategic Reserve Works.
###
### Style: docs/guides/gui_style_guide.md. The overview is always shown. The
### inventory is open until closed (st_res_inventory_closed). How the
### Strategic Reserve Works is collapsed until opened (st_res_how_open). Each
### section is a type, and the two composers set their order, so a system tab
### could show the same pieces. Collapse flags say their default: *_closed is
### open until closed, *_open collapsed until opened.
### test_strategic_reserve_layout.py holds the order, the flags and the rows.
###
### Icons: the hub cell uses the hub building's own icon; the row's policy
### icon is a vanilla placeholder. docs/systems/strategic_reserve_gui_icons.md
### lists both, with the final art the placeholder should become.
###
### THE INVENTORY is a table with one te_st_res_good_row per unlocked good:
###   Good | Stock | Status | policy icon | decrease / stop / increase
### Stock is the fill bar, with a marker at the policy's target stockpile while
### it can buy and at its protected stockpile while it can sell. The policy
### icon is lit while an automated policy sets the good's rate. Clicking the
### good's name expands the row: its figures as label / value rows, its policy
### and why the policy is doing what it does, and a collapsed Policy Settings
### subsection holding the policy panel.
###
### Data contract. Everything the rows show comes from script; nothing is
### re-derived here:
###   - row visibility  -> ScriptedGui.IsShown, which delegates to
###                        st_res_<good>_unlocked_trigger
###                        (common/scripted_triggers/st_res_triggers.txt)
###   - button enabled  -> ScriptedGui.IsValid (cap / stockpile-room checks)
###   - status label    -> GetCustom('st_res_<good>_mode_text'), driven by the
###                        st_res_<good>_last_status variable written by
###                        st_res_set_good_status_effect
###   - fill bar        -> ScriptValue('st_res_<good>_fill_pct')
###   - bar markers     -> ScriptValue('st_res_<good>_disp_target') and
###                        ScriptValue('st_res_<good>_disp_floor'), which sit at
###                        the bar's ends (and so hide) unless the policy uses
###                        that bound
###   - policy icon     -> ScriptValue('st_res_<good>_disp_policy'), the policy
###                        code
###   - net movement    -> ScriptValue('st_res_<good>_last_net'), i.e. the
###                        post-clamp delta recorded by the weekly pulse
###   - decay rate      -> ScriptValue('st_res_<good>_annual_decay_rate'), the
###                        same value the weekly bookkeeping divides by 52,
###                        and ScriptValue('st_res_<good>_weekly_decay')
###   - hub icon        -> ScriptValue('st_res_disp_hub_staffed')
### The display values are in the "Panel display values" group of
### common/script_values/st_res_script_values.txt; no script reads them.
###
### The three rate controls share one scripted GUI per good and differ only by
### the 'dir' saved scope (0 = decrease, 1 = stop, 2 = increase). Adding a good
### means one new te_st_res_good_row instance in te_st_res_sec_inventory, plus
### the script, loc and scripted GUIs listed in
### .claude/skills/add-strategic-reserve-good/SKILL.md.
###
### RESERVE POLICIES (the expanded figures and the Policy Settings subsection)
###   - policy name    -> GetCustom('st_res_<good>_policy_text'), driven by the
###                       st_res_<good>_policy variable
###   - explanation    -> GetCustom('st_res_<good>_policy_reason_text'), driven
###                       by st_res_<good>_policy_status, whose single
###                       derivation site is st_res_policy_evaluate_good_effect
###   - price signal   -> ScriptValue('st_res_<good>_price_rel'), the live
###                       signed premium against base price on the country's
###                       own market, and ScriptValue('st_res_<good>_price_signal'),
###                       the running average the policy actually acts on
###                       (advanced once a week by script). Nothing here
###                       re-derives either from prices.
###
### The panel's controls share a SECOND scripted GUI per good,
### st_res_policy_<good>_sgui, parameterized by a single 'op' saved scope.
### Both files carry the op-code table; keep them in sync:
###
###   0-3   select policy   Manual / Buy When Cheap / Release When Expensive /
###                         Stabilize Prices. The four buttons use the SHORT
###                         labels (st_res_policy_short_*) so they fit the
###                         104px button; the expanded figures and the
###                         tooltips carry the full names.
###   10-12 apply preset    Conservative / Standard / Aggressive
###   20/21 purchase threshold  - / +      26/27 protected stockpile - / +
###   22/23 release threshold   - / +      28/29 target stockpile    - / +
###   24/25 maximum weekly flow - / +      30/31 weekly budget       - / +
###   32/33 price memory (weeks) - / +     34/35 response ramp (pp)  - / +
###   44/45 maximum weekly flow ten steps  50/51 weekly budget ten steps
###   64/65 maximum weekly flow 100 steps  70/71 weekly budget 100 steps
###
### The flow and budget steppers carry click_modifiers: shift-click is the
### plain op + 20, ctrl-click the plain op + 40. `enabled` stays bound to the
### plain op, whose is_valid branch the modifier ops share.
###
### Every expander is presentation-only: `GetVariableSystem.Toggle` on a key
### that no script ever reads, not saved. Collapsing a row, its settings or a
### section cannot change what the reserve does, and policies keep running
### with the journal entry closed because the evaluator lives on the weekly
### pulse, not in this file.

types strategic_reserve_widget_types
{
	### ======================================================================
	### BUILDING BLOCKS. The UN's (un_chamber_widget.gui), copied under this
	### system's prefix so neither file depends on the other.
	### ======================================================================

	### A section's body: the dark panel under its header.
	type st_res_panel = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		parentanchor = hcenter
		margin = { 20 8 }
		spacing = 4

		background = {
			using = entry_bg_fancy_dark
			alpha = 0.5
		}
	}

	type st_res_section_header = section_header_button {
		blockoverride "layout" {
			parentanchor = hcenter
			size = { 520 38 }
		}
	}

	### A collapsible subsection inside a row: narrower, lower and in a
	### smaller type than a section header, so it reads as part of the row
	### (un_chamber_subsection_header's shape, gui_modding_guide.md gotcha #26).
	type st_res_subsection_header = section_header_button {
		blockoverride "layout" {
			size = { 430 30 }
		}
		blockoverride "fontsize" {
			using = fontsize_medium
		}
		blockoverride "arrow_size" {
			size = { 20 20 }
		}
		blockoverride "left_textbox_margin_left" {
			margin_left = 32
		}
	}

	### A heading over one group of lines, with a faint rule under it.
	type st_res_subheader = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 1
		block "subheader_margin" {
			margin_top = 10
		}

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			multiline = yes
			maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_large
			default_format = "#title"
			block "subheader_text" {}
		}
		divider_clean = {
			blockoverride "size" {
				size = { 480 2 }
			}
		}
	}

	### Explanatory text under a heading: how a part works, rather than what
	### it says now. Static keys only.
	type st_res_note = textbox {
		autoresize = yes
		multiline = yes
		minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
		maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
		align = left|nobaseline
		using = fontsize_medium
		default_format = "#lore"
	}

	### A table row: a label on the left, its value on the right. Sized for a
	### good's expanded figures, set in 24px under the good's name:
	### 4 + 170 + 270 + 4 = 448 of the 456 left.
	type st_res_value_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		margin = { 4 1 }

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 170 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 170 -1 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_medium
			elide = right
			block "row_label" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 270 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 270 -1 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_medium
			default_format = "#v"
			elide = right
			block "row_value" {}
		}
	}

	### A column heading over the inventory: small, and underlined where it
	### has a tooltip.
	type st_res_col_heading = textbox {
		autoresize = no
		align = left|nobaseline
		using = fontsize_small
		elide = right
		parentanchor = vcenter
	}

	### ======================================================================
	### THE OVERVIEW. Always shown, at the top (container 1).
	### ======================================================================

	### A cell of the overview: its icon or figure on top, its word small
	### beneath. Fixed width, so a long word cannot push the row wider.
	type st_res_ov_cell = widget {
		size = { 130 58 }

		block "cell_top" {}

		textbox = {
			parentanchor = bottom|hcenter
			autoresize = yes
			max_width = 128
			elide = right
			align = hcenter|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_small
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			block "label" {}
		}
	}

	### The figure on top of an overview cell.
	type st_res_ov_figure = textbox {
		parentanchor = top|hcenter
		position = { 0 8 }
		autoresize = yes
		max_width = 128
		elide = right
		align = hcenter|nobaseline
		using = fontsize_large
		default_format = "#v"
	}

	### The hub, the flow cap and the week's sales income: what a returning
	### player checks before reading the rows. The first two lines of the old
	### status text (income, flow cap) moved here, their explanations into
	### the cells' tooltips.
	type te_st_res_overview_panel = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"

		st_res_panel = {
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = horizontal
				spacing = 12
				parentanchor = hcenter

				### The hub: its own icon, at full colour while it is fully
				### staffed and dimmed below that, when it trades nothing. The
				### dimmed icon is always drawn; the lit one covers it.
				st_res_ov_cell = {
					tooltip = "je_strategic_reserve_ov_hub_tt"
					blockoverride "cell_top" {
						icon = {
							size = { 36 36 }
							parentanchor = top|hcenter
							alpha = 0.3
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/building_icons/building_strategic_reserve_hub.dds"
						}
						icon = {
							size = { 36 36 }
							parentanchor = top|hcenter
							visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('st_res_disp_hub_staffed'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/building_icons/building_strategic_reserve_hub.dds"
						}
					}
					blockoverride "label" {
						text = "[SelectLocalization( EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('st_res_disp_hub_staffed'), '(CFixedPoint)1' ), 'je_strategic_reserve_ov_hub_staffed', 'je_strategic_reserve_ov_hub_understaffed' )]"
					}
				}

				### How much of one good the hub may move in a week.
				st_res_ov_cell = {
					tooltip = "je_strategic_reserve_ov_cap_tt"
					blockoverride "cell_top" {
						st_res_ov_figure = {
							text = "je_strategic_reserve_ov_cap_value"
						}
					}
					blockoverride "label" {
						text = "je_strategic_reserve_ov_cap_label"
					}
				}

				### What this week's releases earn.
				st_res_ov_cell = {
					tooltip = "je_strategic_reserve_ov_income_tt"
					blockoverride "cell_top" {
						st_res_ov_figure = {
							text = "je_strategic_reserve_ov_income_value"
						}
					}
					blockoverride "label" {
						text = "je_strategic_reserve_ov_income_label"
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### ======================================================================
	### THE INVENTORY (container 2)
	### ======================================================================

	### One control in the policy selector or the preset row. The op code is the
	### same for every good, so this template is fully shared: which good a click
	### lands on comes from the policy panel's datacontext, not from the button.
	type widget_je_st_res_policy_choice = button {
		using = default_button_action
		size = { 104 26 }

		textbox = {
			parentanchor = center
			align = center|nobaseline
			autoresize = yes
			max_width = 96
			elide = right
			using = fontsize_small
			block "choice_label" {}
		}

		block "choice_action" {}
	}

	### One settings row: label, minus, current value, plus. `stepper_value` is
	### the only per-good part; every panel instance overrides it with that
	### good's variable, and the two op codes stay shared.
	### 240 + 24 + 110 + 24 and three 3px gaps: 407.
	type widget_je_st_res_policy_stepper = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		spacing = 3

		textbox = {
			block "stepper_label" {}
			size = { 240 24 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_small
			parentanchor = vcenter
			elide = right
		}

		button_icon_minus_action = {
			size = { 24 24 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			block "stepper_down" {}
		}

		textbox = {
			block "stepper_value" {}
			size = { 110 24 }
			align = center|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_small
			parentanchor = vcenter
			elide = right
		}

		button_icon_plus_action = {
			size = { 24 24 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			block "stepper_up" {}
		}
	}

	### The per-good settings panel, under a row's Policy Settings subsection.
	### The row shows it only while that subsection is open (the good's
	### st_res_policy_<good>_open key).
	###
	### Everything inside is shared across goods except the eight value cells:
	### `policy_panel_context` points the whole subtree at that good's
	### st_res_policy_<good>_sgui, and every button below addresses it by op
	### code alone. The op-code table lives in
	### common/scripted_guis/st_res_scripted_gui.txt — keep the two in sync.
	### 424 wide inside a 6px margin: 436 of the 456 the row's figures leave.
	type widget_je_st_res_policy_panel = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		spacing = 3
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		margin = { 6 6 }

		background = {
			using = blurry_dark_background
			alpha = 0.75
		}

		block "policy_panel_context" {}

		textbox = {
			text = "st_res_policy_panel_policy_header"
			size = { 424 22 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_small
			elide = right
		}

		### Policy selector — ops 0-3. The button for the policy already in
		### force is disabled by is_valid, which doubles as the "you are here"
		### indicator.
		flowcontainer = {
			direction = horizontal
			spacing = 3

			widget_je_st_res_policy_choice = {
				blockoverride "choice_label" { text = "st_res_policy_short_manual" }
				blockoverride "choice_action" {
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "st_res_policy_manual_tooltip"
				}
			}
			widget_je_st_res_policy_choice = {
				blockoverride "choice_label" { text = "st_res_policy_short_buy_cheap" }
				blockoverride "choice_action" {
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "st_res_policy_buy_cheap_tooltip"
				}
			}
			widget_je_st_res_policy_choice = {
				blockoverride "choice_label" { text = "st_res_policy_short_release_high" }
				blockoverride "choice_action" {
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "st_res_policy_release_high_tooltip"
				}
			}
			widget_je_st_res_policy_choice = {
				blockoverride "choice_label" { text = "st_res_policy_short_stabilize" }
				blockoverride "choice_action" {
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)3' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "st_res_policy_stabilize_tooltip"
				}
			}
		}

		### What a preset does is on the heading's hover (style rule 3).
		textbox = {
			text = "st_res_policy_panel_preset_header"
			tooltip = "st_res_policy_panel_preset_header_tt"
			size = { 424 22 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_small
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			elide = right
		}

		### Presets — ops 10-12. Each fills all eight settings at once. The
		### button of the preset in force is disabled by is_valid, like the
		### policy selector's, until a stepper changes a setting by hand.
		flowcontainer = {
			direction = horizontal
			spacing = 3

			widget_je_st_res_policy_choice = {
				blockoverride "choice_label" { text = "st_res_preset_conservative" }
				blockoverride "choice_action" {
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)10' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)10' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "st_res_preset_conservative_tooltip"
				}
			}
			widget_je_st_res_policy_choice = {
				blockoverride "choice_label" { text = "st_res_preset_standard" }
				blockoverride "choice_action" {
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)11' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)11' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "st_res_preset_standard_tooltip"
				}
			}
			widget_je_st_res_policy_choice = {
				blockoverride "choice_label" { text = "st_res_preset_aggressive" }
				blockoverride "choice_action" {
					enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)12' ) ).End )]"
					onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)12' ) ).End )]"
					tooltip = "st_res_preset_aggressive_tooltip"
				}
			}
		}

		textbox = {
			text = "st_res_policy_panel_settings_header"
			size = { 424 22 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_small
			elide = right
		}

		widget_je_st_res_policy_stepper = {
			blockoverride "stepper_label" { text = "st_res_policy_label_buy_thr" }
			blockoverride "stepper_value" { block "policy_value_buy_thr" {} }
			blockoverride "stepper_down" {
				enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)20' ) ).End )]"
				onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)20' ) ).End )]"
				tooltip = "st_res_policy_label_buy_thr_down_tooltip"
			}
			blockoverride "stepper_up" {
				enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)21' ) ).End )]"
				onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)21' ) ).End )]"
				tooltip = "st_res_policy_label_buy_thr_up_tooltip"
			}
		}
		widget_je_st_res_policy_stepper = {
			blockoverride "stepper_label" { text = "st_res_policy_label_sell_thr" }
			blockoverride "stepper_value" { block "policy_value_sell_thr" {} }
			blockoverride "stepper_down" {
				enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)22' ) ).End )]"
				onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)22' ) ).End )]"
				tooltip = "st_res_policy_label_sell_thr_down_tooltip"
			}
			blockoverride "stepper_up" {
				enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)23' ) ).End )]"
				onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)23' ) ).End )]"
				tooltip = "st_res_policy_label_sell_thr_up_tooltip"
			}
		}
		widget_je_st_res_policy_stepper = {
			blockoverride "stepper_label" { text = "st_res_policy_label_max_flow" }
			blockoverride "stepper_value" { block "policy_value_max_flow" {} }
			blockoverride "stepper_down" {
				enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)24' ) ).End )]"
				### Click one step, shift-click ten, ctrl-click a hundred.
				click_modifiers = {
					ondefault = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)24' ) ).End )]"
					onshift = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)44' ) ).End )]"
					onctrl = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)64' ) ).End )]"
				}
				tooltip = "st_res_policy_label_max_flow_down_tooltip"
			}
			blockoverride "stepper_up" {
				enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)25' ) ).End )]"
				### Click one step, shift-click ten, ctrl-click a hundred.
				click_modifiers = {
					ondefault = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)25' ) ).End )]"
					onshift = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)45' ) ).End )]"
					onctrl = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)65' ) ).End )]"
				}
				tooltip = "st_res_policy_label_max_flow_up_tooltip"
			}
		}
		widget_je_st_res_policy_stepper = {
			blockoverride "stepper_label" { text = "st_res_policy_label_floor_pct" }
			blockoverride "stepper_value" { block "policy_value_floor_pct" {} }
			blockoverride "stepper_down" {
				enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)26' ) ).End )]"
				onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)26' ) ).End )]"
				tooltip = "st_res_policy_label_floor_pct_down_tooltip"
			}
			blockoverride "stepper_up" {
				enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)27' ) ).End )]"
				onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)27' ) ).End )]"
				tooltip = "st_res_policy_label_floor_pct_up_tooltip"
			}
		}
		widget_je_st_res_policy_stepper = {
			blockoverride "stepper_label" { text = "st_res_policy_label_ceil_pct" }
			blockoverride "stepper_value" { block "policy_value_ceil_pct" {} }
			blockoverride "stepper_down" {
				enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)28' ) ).End )]"
				onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)28' ) ).End )]"
				tooltip = "st_res_policy_label_ceil_pct_down_tooltip"
			}
			blockoverride "stepper_up" {
				enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)29' ) ).End )]"
				onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)29' ) ).End )]"
				tooltip = "st_res_policy_label_ceil_pct_up_tooltip"
			}
		}
		widget_je_st_res_policy_stepper = {
			blockoverride "stepper_label" { text = "st_res_policy_label_budget" }
			blockoverride "stepper_value" { block "policy_value_budget" {} }
			blockoverride "stepper_down" {
				enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)30' ) ).End )]"
				### Click one step, shift-click ten, ctrl-click a hundred.
				click_modifiers = {
					ondefault = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)30' ) ).End )]"
					onshift = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)50' ) ).End )]"
					onctrl = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)70' ) ).End )]"
				}
				tooltip = "st_res_policy_label_budget_down_tooltip"
			}
			blockoverride "stepper_up" {
				enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)31' ) ).End )]"
				### Click one step, shift-click ten, ctrl-click a hundred.
				click_modifiers = {
					ondefault = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)31' ) ).End )]"
					onshift = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)51' ) ).End )]"
					onctrl = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)71' ) ).End )]"
				}
				tooltip = "st_res_policy_label_budget_up_tooltip"
			}
		}
		widget_je_st_res_policy_stepper = {
			blockoverride "stepper_label" { text = "st_res_policy_label_price_memory" }
			blockoverride "stepper_value" { block "policy_value_price_memory" {} }
			blockoverride "stepper_down" {
				enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)32' ) ).End )]"
				onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)32' ) ).End )]"
				tooltip = "st_res_policy_label_price_memory_down_tooltip"
			}
			blockoverride "stepper_up" {
				enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)33' ) ).End )]"
				onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)33' ) ).End )]"
				tooltip = "st_res_policy_label_price_memory_up_tooltip"
			}
		}
		widget_je_st_res_policy_stepper = {
			blockoverride "stepper_label" { text = "st_res_policy_label_ramp" }
			blockoverride "stepper_value" { block "policy_value_ramp" {} }
			blockoverride "stepper_down" {
				enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)34' ) ).End )]"
				onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)34' ) ).End )]"
				tooltip = "st_res_policy_label_ramp_down_tooltip"
			}
			blockoverride "stepper_up" {
				enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)35' ) ).End )]"
				onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)35' ) ).End )]"
				tooltip = "st_res_policy_label_ramp_up_tooltip"
			}
		}
	}

	### One good's row: the table line, and under it, while the row is
	### expanded, the good's figures and its Policy Settings. Every good's
	### instance has the same shape, a copy of another good's with the good's
	### name swapped (.claude/skills/add-strategic-reserve-good). The instance
	### supplies:
	###   datacontext           GetScriptedGui('st_res_adjust_<good>_sgui')
	###   visible               that scripted GUI's IsShown (the unlock trigger)
	###   tooltip               st_res_row_<good>_tooltip, the whole breakdown
	###   row_toggle, row_open, row_closed
	###                         the row's st_res_row_<good>_open key
	###   row_name, row_status  loc keys
	###   row_fill              the bar's value, st_res_<good>_fill_pct
	###   row_target_marker, row_floor_marker
	###                         each marker's value and its visible
	###   row_auto              the lit policy icon's visible
	###   row_stored ... row_policy, row_policy_reason
	###                         the expanded figures (loc keys)
	###   row_settings_toggle, row_settings_open, row_settings_closed
	###                         the settings' st_res_policy_<good>_open key
	###   row_policy_panel      the good's widget_je_st_res_policy_panel
	### The three rate buttons read the inherited ScriptedGui, so they are the
	### same for every good.
	type te_st_res_good_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 2

		### The table line. 130 + 114 + 96 + 26 + 3 x 26, with seven 4px gaps,
		### is 472 of the panel's 480; the column headings' widths match.
		flowcontainer = {
			direction = horizontal
			spacing = 4

			### Good: an untextured button, so the name reads as plain text and
			### a click expands or collapses the row. The chevron left of the
			### name is vanilla's outliner pair (gui/outliner_framework.gui):
			### expand_arrow while collapsed, expand_arrow_expanded while
			### expanded. Both are alwaystransparent, so chevron and name are one
			### click target. Its tooltip replaces the row's over the name only.
			button = {
				size = { 130 28 }
				parentanchor = vcenter
				block "row_toggle" {}

				button = {
					using = expand_arrow
					size = { 20 20 }
					parentanchor = left|vcenter
					alwaystransparent = yes
					block "row_closed" {}
				}
				button = {
					using = expand_arrow_expanded
					size = { 20 20 }
					parentanchor = left|vcenter
					alwaystransparent = yes
					block "row_open" {}
				}
				textbox = {
					position = { 20 0 }
					size = { 110 28 }
					align = left|nobaseline
					using = fontsize_medium
					elide = right
					block "row_name" {}
				}
			}

			### Stock: the fill against capacity (0-100). A marker stands at the
			### target stockpile while the policy can buy and at the protected
			### stockpile while it can sell; the instance hides each at its end
			### of the bar, where st_res_<good>_disp_* put it when the policy
			### does not use that bound. The marker technique is the UN
			### authority bar's (un_overview_widget.gui).
			widget = {
				size = { 114 28 }
				parentanchor = vcenter

				default_progressbar_horizontal = {
					size = { 114 18 }
					parentanchor = vcenter
					blockoverride "values" {
						block "row_fill" {}
						min = 0
						max = 100
					}
					blockoverride "on_top_of_the_progressbar" {
						progressbar = {
							noprogresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
							progresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
							size = { 100% 100% }
							skip_initial_animation = yes
							direction = horizontal
							min = 0
							max = 100
							block "row_target_marker" {}
							marker = {
								icon = {
									size = { 36 20 }
									parentanchor = vcenter
									widgetanchor = center
									texture = "gfx/interface/progressbar/progressbar_marker.dds"
								}
							}
						}
						progressbar = {
							noprogresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
							progresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
							size = { 100% 100% }
							skip_initial_animation = yes
							direction = horizontal
							min = 0
							max = 100
							block "row_floor_marker" {}
							marker = {
								icon = {
									size = { 36 20 }
									parentanchor = vcenter
									widgetanchor = center
									texture = "gfx/interface/progressbar/progressbar_marker.dds"
								}
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}

			### Status: Storing / Withdrawing / Idle / Blocked, coloured. The
			### reason is on the row's tooltip.
			textbox = {
				size = { 96 28 }
				parentanchor = vcenter
				align = left|nobaseline
				using = fontsize_medium
				elide = right
				block "row_status" {}
			}

			### Policy: lit while an automated reserve policy sets this good's
			### rate, dimmed on Manual. The dimmed icon is always drawn; the lit
			### one covers it (`row_auto` is its visible).
			widget = {
				size = { 26 28 }
				parentanchor = vcenter
				tooltip = "st_res_row_auto_tooltip"

				icon = {
					size = { 24 24 }
					parentanchor = center
					alpha = 0.25
					texture = "gfx/interface/production_methods/auto_expand.dds"
				}
				icon = {
					size = { 24 24 }
					parentanchor = center
					block "row_auto" {}
					texture = "gfx/interface/production_methods/auto_expand.dds"
				}
			}

			### Decrease — dir 0
			button_icon_minus_action = {
				size = { 26 26 }
				parentanchor = vcenter
				visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'dir', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
				enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'dir', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
				onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'dir', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
				tooltip = "st_res_row_decrease_tooltip"
			}

			### Stop — dir 1
			button_icon_cancel = {
				size = { 26 26 }
				parentanchor = vcenter
				visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'dir', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
				enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'dir', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
				onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'dir', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
				tooltip = "st_res_row_stop_tooltip"
			}

			### Increase — dir 2
			button_icon_plus_action = {
				size = { 26 26 }
				parentanchor = vcenter
				visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'dir', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End )]"
				enabled = "[ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'dir', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End )]"
				onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'dir', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)2' ) ).End )]"
				tooltip = "st_res_row_increase_tooltip"
			}
		}

		### The good's figures, while the row is expanded: label and value rows
		### (style rule 5), set in under the name. `row_open` is the same block
		### the expanded chevron reads.
		flowcontainer = {
			direction = vertical
			ignoreinvisible = yes
			spacing = 1
			margin_left = 24
			margin_bottom = 6
			block "row_open" {}

			st_res_value_row = {
				blockoverride "row_label" { text = "st_res_row_label_stored" }
				blockoverride "row_value" { block "row_stored" {} }
			}
			st_res_value_row = {
				blockoverride "row_label" { text = "st_res_row_label_rate" }
				blockoverride "row_value" { block "row_rate" {} }
			}
			st_res_value_row = {
				blockoverride "row_label" { text = "st_res_row_label_last" }
				blockoverride "row_value" { block "row_last" {} }
			}
			st_res_value_row = {
				blockoverride "row_label" { text = "st_res_row_label_decay" }
				blockoverride "row_value" { block "row_decay" {} }
			}
			st_res_value_row = {
				blockoverride "row_label" { text = "st_res_row_label_price" }
				blockoverride "row_value" { block "row_price" {} }
			}
			st_res_value_row = {
				blockoverride "row_label" { text = "st_res_row_label_policy" }
				blockoverride "row_value" { block "row_policy" {} }
			}

			### What the policy is doing this week, and why. Straight from
			### st_res_<good>_policy_status via customizable localization; the
			### GUI never works out why a lane is paused.
			textbox = {
				autoresize = yes
				multiline = yes
				minimumsize = { 440 -1 }
				maximumsize = { 440 -1 }
				margin = { 4 1 }
				align = left|nobaseline
				using = fontsize_small
				block "row_policy_reason" {}
			}

			### Policy Settings: the policy, the presets and the eight settings.
			### A long subsection, so it starts collapsed (style rule 7).
			st_res_subsection_header = {
				blockoverride "left_text" {
					text = "st_res_row_settings_header"
				}
				blockoverride "onclick" {
					block "row_settings_toggle" {}
				}
				blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
					block "row_settings_closed" {}
				}
				blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
					block "row_settings_open" {}
				}
			}
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = vertical
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				block "row_settings_open" {}

				block "row_policy_panel" {}
			}
		}
	}

	### The inventory: the adjustment step (true of every row's buttons, so
	### said once above them), the column headings, and one row per good.
	### Open until closed.
	type te_st_res_sec_inventory = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4

		st_res_section_header = {
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "je_strategic_reserve_inv_header"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Toggle('st_res_inventory_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
				visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('st_res_inventory_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
				visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('st_res_inventory_closed'))]"
			}
		}

		st_res_panel = {
			visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('st_res_inventory_closed'))]"

			textbox = {
				autoresize = yes
				minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
				maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
				align = left|nobaseline
				using = fontsize_medium
				text = "je_strategic_reserve_inv_step"
			}

			### Column headings, at the row's cell widths (te_st_res_good_row).
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = horizontal
				spacing = 4
				margin_top = 4

				st_res_col_heading = {
					size = { 130 20 }
					margin_left = 20
					text = "je_strategic_reserve_inv_col_good"
				}
				st_res_col_heading = {
					size = { 114 20 }
					default_format = "#tooltippable"
					text = "je_strategic_reserve_inv_col_stock"
					tooltip = "je_strategic_reserve_inv_col_stock_tt"
				}
				st_res_col_heading = {
					size = { 96 20 }
					default_format = "#tooltippable"
					text = "je_strategic_reserve_inv_col_status"
					tooltip = "je_strategic_reserve_inv_col_status_tt"
				}
				### Over the three rate buttons; the policy icon's column has no
				### heading (its tooltip says what it is).
				st_res_col_heading = {
					size = { 116 20 }
					margin_left = 30
					default_format = "#tooltippable"
					text = "je_strategic_reserve_inv_col_rate"
					tooltip = "je_strategic_reserve_inv_col_rate_tt"
				}
			}
			divider_clean = {
				blockoverride "size" {
					size = { 480 2 }
				}
			}

			te_st_res_good_row = {
				datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('st_res_adjust_grain_sgui')]"
				visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'dir', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
				tooltip = "st_res_row_grain_tooltip"

				blockoverride "row_toggle" {
					onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Toggle('st_res_row_grain_open')]"
					tooltip = "st_res_row_collapse_tooltip"
				}
				blockoverride "row_open" {
					visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('st_res_row_grain_open')]"
				}
				blockoverride "row_closed" {
					visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('st_res_row_grain_open'))]"
				}
				blockoverride "row_name" { text = "st_res_row_grain_name" }
				blockoverride "row_status" { text = "st_res_row_grain_status" }
				blockoverride "row_fill" {
					value = "[FixedPointToFloat( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('st_res_grain_fill_pct') )]"
				}
				blockoverride "row_target_marker" {
					visible = "[LessThan_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('st_res_grain_disp_target'), '(CFixedPoint)100' )]"
					value = "[FixedPointToFloat( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('st_res_grain_disp_target') )]"
				}
				blockoverride "row_floor_marker" {
					visible = "[GreaterThan_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('st_res_grain_disp_floor'), '(CFixedPoint)0' )]"
					value = "[FixedPointToFloat( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('st_res_grain_disp_floor') )]"
				}
				blockoverride "row_auto" {
					visible = "[GreaterThan_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('st_res_grain_disp_policy'), '(CFixedPoint)0' )]"
				}
				blockoverride "row_stored" { text = "st_res_row_grain_amount" }
				blockoverride "row_rate" { text = "st_res_row_grain_flow" }
				blockoverride "row_last" { text = "st_res_row_grain_last" }
				blockoverride "row_decay" { text = "st_res_row_grain_decay" }
				blockoverride "row_price" { text = "st_res_row_grain_price" }
				blockoverride "row_policy" { text = "st_res_row_grain_policy" }
				blockoverride "row_policy_reason" { text = "st_res_row_grain_policy_reason" }
				blockoverride "row_settings_toggle" {
					onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Toggle('st_res_policy_grain_open')]"
				}
				blockoverride "row_settings_open" {
					visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('st_res_policy_grain_open')]"
				}
				blockoverride "row_settings_closed" {
					visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('st_res_policy_grain_open'))]"
				}
				blockoverride "row_policy_panel" {
					widget_je_st_res_policy_panel = {
						blockoverride "policy_panel_context" {
							datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('st_res_policy_grain_sgui')]"
						}
						blockoverride "policy_value_buy_thr" {
							text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('st_res_grain_buy_thr').GetValue|+0]"
						}
						blockoverride "policy_value_sell_thr" {
							text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('st_res_grain_sell_thr').GetValue|+0]"
						}
						blockoverride "policy_value_max_flow" {
							text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('st_res_grain_max_flow').GetValue|0]"
						}
						blockoverride "policy_value_floor_pct" {
							text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('st_res_grain_floor_pct').GetValue|0]"
						}
						blockoverride "policy_value_ceil_pct" {
							text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('st_res_grain_ceil_pct').GetValue|0]"
						}
						blockoverride "policy_value_budget" {
							text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('st_res_grain_budget').GetValue|0]"
						}
						blockoverride "policy_value_price_memory" {
							text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('st_res_grain_price_memory').GetValue|0]"
						}
						blockoverride "policy_value_ramp" {
							text = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('st_res_grain_ramp').GetValue|0]"
						}
					}
				}
			}

			te_st_res_good_row = {
				datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('st_res_adjust_ammunition_sgui')]"
				visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'dir', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
				tooltip = "st_res_row_ammunition_tooltip"

				blockoverride "row_toggle" {
					onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Toggle('st_res_row_ammunition_open')]"
					tooltip = "st_res_row_collapse_tooltip"
